<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34009" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pascha</span></b> , ae, f., and
			ătis, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάσχα</span> (Hebr. ). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The feast of the Passover</i>, <i>Easter</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sollennibus Paschae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. ad Uxor. 2, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lege dedit pascham,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. in Carm. adv. Marc. 2, 80</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pascharum dies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Symm. Ep. 10, 77</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dominicum pascha celebrare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 96</span></i>
			, n. 20: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">post sanctum pascha,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 10, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">paschate vicino,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. in Matt. 26, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per tria paschata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. in Dan. 9, 24</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The paschal lamb</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1 Cor.
				5, 7</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">id. Marc. 14, 12</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
